 shown to  correlate  with the number of her2 gene copy  numbers  the mtp chip is integrated  in an automated device that is called  labset research  regions are simply loaded in  eight standard eppendorf and buffers are  stored in  four falcon tubes the chip  is placed in a staining chamber  maintained by a lid  ready to be clamped against a slide  another important microfluidic element  of the system  is the distribution ship it acts as a  gateway between the reservoirs  and the chamber and ensures the proper  control of the flow  towards the tissue reagents  are pushed from the reservoir towards  the distribution system  from where their dispense is controlled  to the staining chamber once the region  is finished  reagents are simply discarded to a  liquid waste  after having tested and proven the  efficiency of the  mtp on single markers immunofluorescence  and hypnosisochemistry we decided to  move towards  multiplexing assays there is an  important drive towards multiplexing  techniques  as the context of personalized medicine  requires even higher number  of markers to be investigated in order  to build better diagnostics  multiplexing immunofluorescence and  immunohistochemistry in particular  are interesting as they allow for  simultaneous marker detection  while keeping the information of  morphological context  that is especially relevant in the study  of the interaction between the tumor and  its micro  environment so the method  chosen uh to do immuno for instance  multiplexing on lab set  is the tyramid signal amplification tsa  this technique allows simultaneous  marker detection on the same tissue  the working principle is the following  so on  your first antigen of interest you would  detect using a primary antibody that you  would bind  with a secondary antibody conjugated to  an enzyme  here a horseradish peroxidase that in  turn  will catalyze the reaction of a tyramid  for a conjugate that binds to the  tuberosine residues  at the antigen site before moving  to the next marker detection the  antibodies need to be removed  by application of heat on the tissue  this step  is called elusion the covalent bound  between the rosin and the teramide  ensures that the signal  stays on the tissue even after the  elusion step  then next subsequent markers can be  detected using the same method  but and just by applying a different  flow form  this can be repeated for all the markers  in  a panel and once  all the termites are bound the slide is  ready for imaging  the tsa kit chosen for this project is  the widely used  opel kit from aquaria biosciences and  the goal was to adapt  these reagents to the lab set system  we use the seven color manual detection  uh  for six markers plus uh conscious  staining  uh with floor fours uh of excitation  wavelengths  ranging from 520 to 690 nanometers  so our objective is to um  automatize a full six plex using the  opel kit and um while the  pre-processing meaning the perfect  departurization  rehydration of the tissue as well as  imaging  will still be done outside a lab set  the machine will take on all the steps  that are directly  related to the staining itself starting  with the heat induced epitope retrieval  uh pruning blocking primary antibody  secondary antibody  and the tsa itself then elusion  all those steps being repeated in the  number of times corresponding to the  detected markers and finally country  staining  the sa development process was organized  around four main axes  the first one the singleplex  optimization  for each marker with the objective to  reach  good and repeatable performance for  every marker individually  the second axis is the uniformity  optimization  with the aim to obtain homogeneous  signal levels over the tissue  even over large sections and then the  antibody elusion optimization  to make the heat induced strip off  reach complete antibody removal between  cycles  while preserving the tissue morphology  at the same time  and finally 