 automation of  vocals on that system  now the uniformity axis uniformity of  the fluorescent signal is an important  feature  of an optimized protocol that can be  challenging  to obtain some time especially on large  tissue sections  labsat offers some interesting  functionalities  that help obtaining a better uniformity  when using a standard incubation of the  reagent on the tissue  depending on the method that is applied  this can lead to an  inhomogeneity in the signal level across  your tissue  labset allows for an active control of  the flow during the incubation  the liquid motion in the chamber can be  controlled at any time  ensuring a more uniform distribution of  the reagent over the tissue  this method called dynamic incubation  increased significantly the level of  uniformity  of stainings done on lab set  we assessed the efficiency of dynamic  incubation  by looking at the signal gradient on  slides incubated in a standard fashion  versus  the slides that we're applying the  dynamic incubation method and  we saw that over one centimeter of  tissue the signal drop  was reduced down to six percent uh when  using dynamic incubation  compared to 30 percent with a standard  incubation  which represents a significant  improvement in uniformity  the third axis of the project is the  elusion optimization  the role of the elusion step is to  ensure a proper removal of  the primary secondary antibody complex  between  two marker detections the method that we  use on labsad  is simply applying a high  heat to the tissue to assess  the efficiency of this evolution method  we compared a reference  stain slide versus an eluted slide  which simply consists in applying the  illusion process  after primary antibody and secondary  antibody  incubations before re-incubating with  secondary antibody  and the substrate if the illusion is  efficient  no signal should be observed on the  eluted slide  the illusion efficiency was defined as  the signal removal rate  the solution efficiency was tested for  all the markers in the panel  and signal removal rate was over 99  percent  for all the six of them which was  considered  as a performant illusion  since our illusion process involves high  temperature  it was important to test  that the repetition of those each cycles  would have limited impact on tissue  morphology  so we tested uh different repetition  numbers of those heating cycles  for three different uh singleplex  and we could observe no apparent  degradation uh  of the the resulting staining  due to the repetition of the illusion  nuclear morphology  extracellular metrics and epitope  detections  were preserved  the last part of this tonsil  optimization  it's the full six plexus say and  our goal is to build an efficient  workflow with a  minimum number of user interactions  so the tissue preprocessing and region  preparation is handled by the user  then then that then has to load all the  elements  on the machine lab set then perform  fully automatically free marker  detections  then due to limited number of reservoirs  a user intervention is required made  protocol  in order to load the regions needed for  the last  three cycles after what the protocol can  be resumed  and finished finally the slide can be  retrieved at the end of the protocol  mounted and imaged  the final result is a semi-automated  sixplex plus counter staining  that can be achieved in four hours and  12 minutes  the full essay showed adequate marker  detection compared to the single plex  optimization  the conclusion of this first part of the  study  is that the labs that offers a tsa based  multiplexing approach with high signal  intensity for each marker  an adequate signal uniformity across the  tissue section  an efficient antibody illusion with over  99  of signal removal for the six markers  while preserving the tissue morphology  and the epitopes at the same time all  this with a  high level of consistency  so we're now moving to the second part  of the study which is the transfer  of the multiplexing essay on using lab  set  on a different tissue type a cancer  teacher so multiplexing essay  optimized and tonsil can sometimes not  be completely adapted  to other specific tumor sections because  of different marker expression patterns  or sometimes tissue specificities like  different structures  different levels of photoversions etc  the question we ask here is  is this tonsil optimized protocol  applicable to my cancer tissue samples  we approach this with a three-step  transfer strategy  first we applied the tonsil optimized  protocol directly  to our cancer sample then we evaluated  the performance  and defined what needed to be  re-optimized and finally  we modified protocol parameters in order  to reach  the desired performance i'm going to  we're going to go through  um a small case study on non-smoking  lung carcinoma old humor  and teammate sections our objective is  to reach  an acceptable performance on this tissue  in a  minimum number of optimization step  because  our aim is to avoid the re-optimization  from zero  labsat offers the flexibility of  optimization  and some important parameters can be  readjusted  directly from the software interface  like the antenna triple temperature the  incubation  times but also protocols are modular  you can add extra steps like blockings  quenching etc and of course you can  always play with the  standard element of an essay like region  titrations  so um the first phase of the transfer  strategy  we applied the the tonsil optimized  protocol directly  on non-smart cell lung carcinoma samples  ig stainings of the corresponding  tissues are shown  here as references for marker expression  and we could observe that the direct  application of the protocol  on this particular tissue showed lower  intensity levels than expected  for all the markers compared to what we  had on tonsil  which indicates that re-optimization  might be needed  so we applied consecutively two simple  protocol adjustments the first one was  to increase  the antigen retrieval temperature of the  assay  and the second one was to increase opal  540  concentration opal 540 is the terminate  that  termite that we associated with the cd8  and this was enough to rescue the signal  levels and to show appropriate  detections for  all the markers we then apply this  reoptimize six flex  to nsclc tissue microarray  in order to assess the protocol on  various  expression patterns and here the  re-optimized protocol should appropriate  detection  of all the markers on on those  tma cores comparably to the standard ihd  reference  various pattern of expression could be  detected similarly to the iot reference  using this reoptimized protocol  and the total time of the sa remain  remained unchanged  compared to the tonsil optimized  protocol  staying at 4 hours and 12 minutes  so as a conclusion labsat offers the  possibility to run a six flex seven  color sa  in a timely manner with high quality  results  both in terms of signal uniformity strip  off efficiency  and morphology preservation the tonsil  optimized protocol could be transferred  to land cancer tissue for the same assay  duration  and the protocol transfer process was a  simple  two-step adaptation thank you all for  attending this webinar  i encourage you to send all the  questions you might have to the email  address you see below  communication at lunaford.com we'll get  back to you individually  thank you and have a good day

